<title>USA: Johnson Worldwide to acquire Uwatec AG.</title>
<headline>Johnson Worldwide to acquire Uwatec AG.</headline>
<dateline>RACINE, Wis. 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Johnson Worldwide Associates Inc said Wednesday it entered into an agreement to acquire the common stock of Uwatec AG, a privately held company based in Switzerland.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Uwatec manufactures and markets premium dive computers and other diving instruments. Its products are sold primarily under the Aladin and Uwatec trademarks. For the first nine months of 1996, it had sales of about $19 million.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
